<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 1.7 PCT IN AUGUST - NBP.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY RISES 1.7 PCT IN AUGUST - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 2.04</p>
<p>billion zlotys, or 1.7 percent, in August to 121.63 billion</p>
<p>after a 2.3 percent rise in July, preliminary central bank</p>
<p>figures showed.</p>
<p>Broad money supply grew 16.7 percent in the January-August</p>
<p>period against 20.9 percent in the same period of last year.</p>
</text>
